WHAT IS A VLAN:
A VLAN is a separate broadcast domain created on a switch.
It isolates traffic between departments for security and 
performance. Without VLANs a switch floods all frames to 
every port. With VLANs traffic stays within its own VLAN only.
Traffic between VLANs requires a router.

